From: Project SunUEFI <sunuefi@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8750: preserve active PCIe wakeup domains

The PCIe host and QMP PHY mark their devices as an awake path when the
controller retains its link during system suspend. genpd only honours that
request when the provider advertises GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP.

Without that flag both SM8750 PCIe domains collapse even though the host
does not run its deinit/init sequence. On Piano a platform PM test then
leaves the Peach endpoint inaccessible: PCI config and BHI read as all ones,
and ath12k fails its early resume with -ERANGE.

Enable the standard active-wakeup policy for the controller and PHY domains.
This is not an always-on vote: a fully stopped link can still power down.
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8750.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8750.c
@@ -2889,6 +2889,7 @@
 	.collapse_mask = BIT(0),
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_pcie_0_gdsc",
+		.flags = GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP,
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
@@ -2903,6 +2904,7 @@
 	.collapse_mask = BIT(2),
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_pcie_0_phy_gdsc",
+		.flags = GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP,
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
